<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/itagi"><span class="enc-name">Itagi</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Itagi is a village in Koppal district, Karnataka, India, known for the Mahadeva Temple built in 1112 by Mahadeva, a general of the Western Chalukya king Vikramaditya VI.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/itaipu-dam"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/itaipu-dam.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Itaipu Dam</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Itaipu Dam is a hydroelectric dam on the Paraná River on the border between Brazil and Paraguay, built jointly by the two countries under a treaty of 1973.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/itakh"><span class="enc-name">Itakh</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Itakh al-Khazari was a leading commander of the Turkic army of the Abbasid caliph al-Mu'tasim, a Khazar said to have worked as a slave cook before al-Mu'tasim bought…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/italian-campaign-of-1796-1797"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/italian-campaign-of-1796-1797.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Italian campaign of 1796–1797</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 1796–1797</span><span class="enc-snip">The Italian campaign of 1796–1797 was Napoleon Bonaparte's first great command, in the War of the First Coalition.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/italian-city-states"><span class="enc-name">Italian city-states</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">The Italian city-states were self-governing cities of medieval and Renaissance Italy, such as Venice, Genoa, Pisa and Florence.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/i